## Company Values

### 1. Patient First

| Principle | In Practice |
|-----------|-------------|
| Outcomes over outputs | Measure success by patient health |
| Access over exclusivity | Design for all care settings |
| Safety over speed | Never compromise patient safety |
| Empathy over efficiency | Understand human impact |

**Example**: When designing features, we ask "How does this help a patient?" before "How does this help a user?"

### 2. Trust Through Transparency

| Principle | In Practice |
|-----------|-------------|
| Open communication | Share information freely |
| Honest feedback | Direct, kind, timely |
| Visible decisions | Explain the "why" |
| Admit mistakes | Own problems, fix them fast |

**Example**: We publish our uptime, security certifications, and product roadmap publicly. No spin, no hiding.

### 3. Build to Last

| Principle | In Practice |
|-----------|-------------|
| Quality over quantity | Ship less, ship better |
| Sustainable growth | Don't burn the team |
| Long-term thinking | 10-year decisions |
| Technical excellence | No shortcuts on foundations |

**Example**: We invest in infrastructure and reliability even when customers don't directly ask—because they deserve it.

### 4. Win Together

| Principle | In Practice |
|-----------|-------------|
| Collaboration over competition | Help teammates succeed |
| Shared success | Celebrate team wins |
| Inclusive environment | Every voice matters |
| Customer partnership | Win when they win |

**Example**: No "hero culture"—successes and failures belong to the team, not individuals.

### 5. Iterate with Intent

| Principle | In Practice |
|-----------|-------------|
| Learn fast | Experiment, measure, adjust |
| Data-driven | Decisions backed by evidence |
| Embrace change | Adapt to new information |
| Focus matters | Say no to stay focused |

**Example**: We launch MVPs to learn, but we're deliberate about what we ship to production.

